  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "CMIP6 oxygen is stored per unit volume while WOA23 and the OMZ thresholds are per unit mass, so conversion to micromoles per kilogram is required before any threshold or comparison.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "CMIP6 `o2` is mol m-3; convert to µmol kg-1 as mmol m-3 × 1000/ρ with the in-situ density from `compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None` (not `transform_unit`'s constant default) before applying the 20 and 60 µmol kg-1 thresholds or comparing with WOA23.",
        "A µmol kg-1 threshold applied to the unconverted mol m-3 field marks the whole ocean depleted; take the dissolved oxygen inventory on the volume basis as Σ `o2`·`volcello` (moles, no density), not by integrating a converted per-mass field."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen.md",
      "sha256": "afe46747641c91aff8ddc9f50165a800a7c64d5d2e39b50e816280d02e59fba3",
      "reason": "The WOA23 AOU and percent saturation use their own solubility formula and mass units, while model o2sat/AOU derivations are per volume, so respiration-versus-ventilation interpretation must account for that.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "WOA23 AOU and percent saturation rest on a solubility/pressure convention that need not match the OMIP Garcia and Gordon recipe, so model-observation differences carry a definitional component; CESM2 has no `o2`/`o2sat` in historical (ssp245 only)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "OMZ volumes, total oxygen inventory and within-OMZ means must be weighted by cell volume over all ocean cells rather than simple grid-point averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "OMZ volume is a volume-weighted sum of `volcello` over sub-threshold cells; `compute_exceedance_fraction` leaves missing cells out of numerator and denominator and returns the m3 behind the percentage, and weights must be masked to the same valid cells.",
        "Volume weighting is the Boussinesq protocol form (confirmed for MPIOM only); state the assumption for the other models, and state which basin/region mask each integral used."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "volcello and areacello are needed for cell volumes and layer thickness (volcello/areacello), which underpin OMZ volume, oxygen inventory and maximum OMZ thickness.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "No `thkcello`/`masscello` locally: get column thickness from `cell_thickness_like` (= `volcello`/`areacello`); the `lev_bnds` difference is wrong at partial bottom cells (14 % of GFDL-ESM4 cells differ by >1 %). GFDL-ESM4 `volcello` varies in time; loaders handle the time axis."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The requested Pacific, Indian and Atlantic OMZ volumes depend on the basin partition, and the choice of WOA23 basin mask with marginal seas folded and Southern/Arctic excluded must be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The CMOR Ofx `basin` field is absent; use the WOA23 basin mask (`load_basin_mask`, `select_basin`) with `include_marginal_seas=True` and `depth_dependent=False` (surface labels through the column), and state the mask, Southern Ocean treatment and marginal-sea choice since each changes basin means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "historical-ssp245-member-continuity",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/historical-ssp245-member-continuity.md",
      "sha256": "02341c56015c6296db14585b4561fc32ca6b4e52e2264bec50eee6746c1d55f6",
      "reason": "ssp245 continues the historical member named in parent_variant_label, and the CESM2 local historical/ssp245 member mismatch means no historical-to-ssp245 change can be formed for CESM2.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "CESM2 historical r1i1p1f1 and ssp245 r10i1p1f1 are different realisations (local archive lacks historical r10): no historical baseline exists, so no CESM2 change can be formed — show its ssp245 state only, as the figure plans state.",
        "GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are r1→r1, so their historical-minus-ssp245 (2071-2100 minus 1971-2000) differences and percentage changes are valid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The question uses monthly fields, but OMZ volume and threshold-based thickness are nonlinear diagnostics, so computing them offline from monthly means carries the caveat in this fragment.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Threshold exceedance, OMZ thickness and AOU are nonlinear in monthly means: state whether the diagnostic was formed per month then averaged, or computed from the period mean (average-first matches a climatology reference such as WOA23).",
        "Average the monthly fields over 1971-2000 and 2071-2100 with `temporal_aggregate`, which weights by month length; equal-weight `mean` over time is not the period average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells are marked with 1e20, and any read path that skips CF masking would let those values dominate the volume sums, inventories and means.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "1e20 decodes to NaN via xarray; build each field's valid mask from the field itself (masks differ between variables at the same level) and apply the same mask to the weights.",
        "A hand-written threshold comparison treats NaN as False and counts land in the denominator; use `compute_exceedance_fraction` instead."
      ]
